CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ rethrown exception value preserved: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ outer handler reached after rethrow: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.throw]/8: `throw;` re-propagates the exception being handled to the next
enclosing handler, preserving the exception object.  Non-vacuous.
